†365 /// Always a whole number of tiles.\nL373:     cite367†366 /// A block that ended mid-tile would send its remainder down the eager per-pair path.\nL374:     cite368†367 ///\nL375:     cite369†368 /// That remainder is paid once per block, not once per table, so it has to be zero.\nL376:     cite370†369 #[inline]\nL377:     cite371†370 const fn fused_block<A>() -> usize {\nL378:     cite372†371 // Whole tiles that fit the byte budget at this element width.\nL379:     cite373†372 let whole_tiles = FUSED_BLOCK_BYTES / core::mem::size_of::<A>() / K * K;\nL380:     cite374†373 L381:     cite375†374 // A wide element can exhaust the budget below one tile.\nL382:     cite376†375 // One tile is then the floor.\nL383:     cite377†376 if whole_tiles == 0 { K } else { whole_tiles }\nL384:     cite378†377 }\nL385:     cite379†378 L386:     cite380†379 /// Binds one face of a table in place.\nL387:     cite381†380 ///\nL388:     cite382†381 /// The destination holds the round variable at 0.\nL389:     cite383†382 /// The source holds it at 1.\nL390:     cite384†383 ///\nL391:     cite385†384 /// Each entry becomes the line through the two, sampled at the challenge.\nL1433:     cite1427†1426 debug_assert_eq!(self.sum, self.poly.dot_product());\nL1434:     cite1428†1427 L1435:     cite1429†1428 message\nL1436:     cite1430†1429 }\nL1437:     cite1431†1430 L1438:     cite1432†1431 /// Holds a challenge back for the next measuring pass to absorb.\nL1439:     cite1433†1432 ///\nL1440:     cite1434†1433 /// # Panics\nL1441:     cite1435†1434 ///\nL1442:     cite1436†1435 /// Panics if a challenge is already outstanding.\nL1443:     cite1437†1436 /// Two unapplied bindings cannot be fused into one pass.\nL1444:     cite1438†1437 ///\nL1807:     cite1801†1800 seed in any::<u64>(),\nL1808:     cite1802†1801 ) {\nL1809:     cite1803†1802 let mut rng = SmallRng::seed_from_u64(seed);\nL1810:     cite1804†1803 let (c_a, c_inf, r, claim): (EF, EF, EF, EF) =\nL1811:     cite1805†1804 (rng.random(), rng.random(), rng.random(), rng.random());\nL1812:     cite1806†1805 L1813:     cite1807†1806 // Both reductions are quadratics through {0, 1, inf}; they differ\nL1814:     cite1808†1807 // in which of the three values the round identity supplies.\nL1815:     cite1809†1808 prop_assume!(c_a + c_inf != claim);\nL1816:     cite1810†1809 L1817:     cite1811†1810 prop_assert_ne!(\nL1818:     cite1812†1811 Basis::Evaluation.reduce_claim(c_a, c_inf, r, claim),\nL1819:     cite1813†1812 Basis::Projective.reduce_claim(c_a, c_inf, r, claim),\nL1820:     cite1814†1813 );\nL1821:     cite1815†1814 }\nL1822:     cite1816†1815 }\nL1823:     cite1817†1816 L1824:     cite1818†1817 proptest! {\nL1825:     cite1819†1818 #[test]\nL1826:     cite1820†1819 fn prop_fold_and_round_coefficients_prefix_matches_bind_then_measure(\nL1827:     cite1821†1820 k in 2usize..=16,\nL1828:     cite1822†1821 seed in any::<u64>(),\nL1829:     cite1823†1822 ) {\nL1830:     cite1824†1823 // Invariant: the fused pass is bind-then-measure, in one traversal.\nL1831:     cite1825†1824 //\nL1832:     cite1826†1825 //     two passes: bind the tables, then measure the bound pair\nL1833:     cite1827†1826 //     fused     : one pass doing both\nL1834:     cite1828†1827 //\nL1835:     cite1829†1828 // Both the bound tables and the message have to come out identical.\nL1836:     cite1830†1829 // A prover on the fused path would otherwise send a different transcript.\nL1837:     cite1831†1830 //\nL1838:     cite1832†1831 // Fixture state: 2^k paired random entries, one random challenge.\nL1839:     cite1833†1832 // The range straddles the 8-wide tiled body and the par-vs-serial split.\nL1840:     cite1834†1833 let mut rng = SmallRng::seed_from_u64(seed);\nL1841:     cite1835†1834 let n = 1usize << k;\nL1842: 